WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.390
In 2022, a census counted 1,900,487
farms in the United States.

2
00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:13.550
About 105,000 of them sold 1
million dollars or more each.

3
00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:21.450
Those farms produced 425.3 billion dollars
of the 543.1 billion dollars of farm

4
00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:22.550
output.

5
00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:28.030
Five years earlier, there
were 2,042,220 farms.

6
00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:30.510
Did people stop wanting to farm?

7
00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:32.310
Did farmland run out?

8
00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:34.910
So how did farming get so big?

9
00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:38.050
In this mission, you'll
follow farming as a business,

10
00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:43.490
from seed and machinery to the store, and
see what new technology does to yields.

11
00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:47.830
Then you'll trace beef from cow-calf farms
through the feedlots of the Great Plains

12
00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:49.410
to the store.

13
00:00:49.460 --> 00:00:53.470
Your mission: explain how
US farming got so big.
